.TH UH7000CTL 1 "July 2026" "tascam-uh7000-linux 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uh7000ctl \- inspect and safely prepare a TASCAM UH-7000 on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uh7000ctl
.RB [ --json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uh7000ctl
reports the UH-7000 USB, ALSA, mixer and safety state.  The device is switched
to USB Audio 2.0 configuration 2 by the installed hot-plug service and uses the
stock snd_usb_audio driver.
.PP
Playback commands fail closed while software loopback, DSP direct monitoring,
physical attenuation, capture baseline, or explicit feedback cannot be
positively verified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show typed device, topology, mixer, effects and safety state.
.TP
.B topology
Show ALSA channel, format, rate and feedback information.
.TP
.B diagnostics
Add verified read-only vendor request 0x49 and page 0x1f00 probes.
.TP
.B selector-status
Read the verified one-byte vendor selector status.
.TP
.BI state-dump " directory"
Write only verified read-only request-0x55 pages and a JSON manifest.
.TP
.BI configure " [kernel-name]"
Run the root-only helper that selects UAC2 configuration 2 and registers the
device ID with snd_usb_audio.
.TP
.B preflight
Evaluate playback safety gates.  Confirmation options are
.BR --speakers-disconnected ,
.BR --attenuated-loopback ,
and
.BR --baseline-peak-dbfs .
.TP
.B playback-plan
Print the per-channel guarded-ramp plan without playing audio.
.TP
.B playback-test
Evaluate all safety gates.  Live execution remains unavailable until native
hardware validation proves DSP direct-monitor readback.
.SH SAFETY
Do not connect outputs to inputs without physical attenuation. Disconnect
speakers and headphones. Unknown direct-monitor state is treated as enabled.
The planned ramp starts at -90 dBFS and aborts at -18 dBFS or growth greater
than 12 dB in a 100 ms guard window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/tascam-uh7000/tascam-uh7000-configure
Root-only UAC2 configuration helper.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/tascam-uh7000-linux/protocol.md
Verified protocol boundary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aplay (1),
.BR arecord (1),
.BR pw-link (1)
